From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi7: 056 把 RAM code 的下载请求切成已知能成功的尺寸

The only firmware transfer that has ever completed on this board is the ROM
patch: 12 KB, one PATCH_START_REQ, ring runs to the end.  The RAM code is
144 KB and its ring never moves - and that is true in every state we can put
the chip in:

  - after the 0x07 jump and the endpoint recovery (default)
  - with the RAM request sent as PATCH_START_REQ instead of
    TARGET_ADDRESS_LEN_REQ (diag_ram_as_patch)
  - with the patch semaphore held across the whole download (diag_ram_sem)
  - with the patch skipped entirely, so nothing ever reset the endpoint and
    the ROM is untouched (diag_skip_patch)

In all four cases the MCU answers the request command and then never fetches
a single descriptor, while the 12 KB download in the same boot fetches and
completes normally.  The remaining variable is the size of the single
request, so this splits each region into slices of a configurable size and
asks for one slice at a time:

  diag_ram_chunk_kb=12  -> 12 KB requests, the size that demonstrably works
  diag_ram_chunk_kb=0   -> untouched behaviour, one request per region

Every slice logs its address and length before it is queued, so the first
slice that is refused pinpoints the limit instead of leaving us to guess.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
---
--- a/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
@@ -59,6 +59,18 @@
 module_param(diag_ram_sem, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_ram_sem, "acquire and release the patch semaphore around the RAM download");
 
+/*
+ * 056: the one download that always completes is the 12 KB ROM patch, the one
+ * that never does is the 144 KB RAM code, and that stays true with the patch
+ * skipped, with 0x05 instead of 0x01 and with the patch semaphore held.  The
+ * only variable left is the size of the single request, so ask for a slice at
+ * a time the size that is known to work and watch the ring.
+ */
+static int diag_ram_chunk_kb;
+module_param(diag_ram_chunk_kb, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_ram_chunk_kb,
+		 "split each RAM region into chunks of this many KiB (0 = one request)");
+
 static int
 mcu_wm_patch_sem_ctrl(struct mtk_hw_dev *dev, bool get)
 {
@@ -822,6 +834,45 @@
 				len_cnt += sec_len;
 			}
 
+		} else if (diag_ram_chunk_kb > 0) {
+			u32 chunk = (u32)diag_ram_chunk_kb * 1024;
+			u32 done = 0;
+
+			if (diag_skip_ram_req)
+				dev_warn(dev->dev,
+					 "diag: chunked download without a request\n");
+
+			while (done < len) {
+				u32 part = min_t(u32, chunk, len - done);
+
+				dev_info(dev->dev,
+					 "diag ram chunk: addr=0x%08x len=%u of %u\n",
+					 addr + done, part, len);
+
+				if (!diag_skip_ram_req) {
+					err = mcu_wm_init_download(dev, addr + done,
+								   part, mode,
+								   MCU_FWDL_TYPE_RAM);
+					if (err) {
+						dev_err(dev->dev,
+							"Download request failed\n");
+						return err;
+					}
+				}
+
+				err = mcu_wm_send_firmware(dev,
+							   data + offset + done,
+							   part);
+				if (err) {
+					dev_err(dev->dev,
+						"WM Failed to send firmware\n");
+					return err;
+				}
+
+				done += part;
+			}
+
+			offset += len;
 		} else {
 			/*
 			 * diag_skip_ram_req: push the RAM code into the FWDL ring
